    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "1. Verbs whose meaning depends on the mood"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        3.4,
        6.4,
        7.2
      ],
      "head": [
        "Verb",
        "Indicative (information)",
        "Subjunctive (influence, emotion)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "decir que",
          "Dice que viene. (He says he is coming.)",
          "Dice que vengas. (He tells you to come.)"
        ],
        [
          "escribir / avisar que",
          "Me avisó que llegaba tarde.",
          "Me avisó que llegara pronto. (asked me to)"
        ],
        [
          "entender / comprender que",
          "Entiendo que tiene prisa. (I gather)",
          "Entiendo que tenga prisa. (I can see why)"
        ],
        [
          "sentir que",
          "Siento que me mira. (I feel that)",
          "Siento que no puedas venir. (I regret)"
        ],
        [
          "esperar que",
          "Espero que vengas. (hope: subjunctive)",
          "Espero que llegue. (always subj. for hope)"
        ],
        [
          "parecer que",
          "Parece que llueve.",
          "No parece que llueva."
        ],
        [
          "creer / pensar que",
          "Creo que viene.",
          "No creo que venga."
        ],
        [
          "suponer que",
          "Supongo que viene.",
          "No supongo que venga."
        ],
        [
          "admitir que",
          "Admite que se equivocó. (he states)",
          "No admite que se equivoque. (accept the idea)"
        ],
        [
          "lo que quiero decir es que",
          "Lo que quiero decir es que llegué tarde.",
          "—"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "Rule of thumb",
      "text": "<b>Indicative</b> = a statement of fact or report. <b>Subjunctive</b> = something to bring about (order, wish), a reaction (emotion, evaluation) or a doubt. Many verbs (decir, avisar, escribir, gritar) take both, with a different meaning."
    },
    {
